# Track bridge 0: a wooden toy railway bridge, 24 m long along z (z -12 to 12), 2.4 m wide and 3.8 m high (60 times life size). Two 8 m ramps (about 24 degrees)
# of pine planks on trestle bents climb to an 8 m deck at 3.5 m, the track (0.3 m of sleepers and rails, as track-curve0) on top to 3.8 m. Under the deck an arch
# along x, 6 m wide in z and 3.2 m clear at its crown, lets the road through between two 1 m piers. Mesh collider (ramps and deck walkable, no side rails).
# The ORIGIN is the middle of the deck on y = 0; the ramps' feet are at z = +-12 where the track is 0.3 m high, like the curves.
